1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 d6 7. Bxc6+ bxc6 8.
d4 Nd7 9. Na3 f6 10. Nc4 Nb6 11. Na5 Bd7 12. c4 O-O 13. Be3 Qe8 14. c5 Nc8 15.
Rc1 Rb8 16. Qc2 Rb5 17. cxd6 Bxd6 18. Nxc6 Ne7 19. dxe5 fxe5 20. Nxe7+ Qxe7 21.
Nd2 Be6 22. Nc4 Rfb8 23. Red1 Qf7 24. b3 Be7 25. f3 Bc5 26. Bxc5 Rxc5 27. Qf2
Qf8 28. Ne3 c6 29. Nf5 Rbb5 30. Rxc5 Qxc5 31. Qxc5 Rxc5 32. Ne3 Ra5 33. Rd2 Ra3
34. Kf2 a5 35. Rb2 a4 36. Nc2 Rxa2 37. Rxa2 Bxb3 38. Rb2 c5 39. Ke3 c4 40. Kd2
{"Khassin, who lost both legs in the battle of Stalingrad and walks on two
artificial legs, was an athlete before his misfor- tune but, not unnaturally,
tires rather easily now. He started with four wins but scored only four draws,
one loss thereafter. Littlewood loses a pawn through Khassin’s superior 
(more up-to-date) opening play, and never gets on even terms." (CHESS)} 1-0

