Nc6 9. Ne5 e6 10. Nxc6 bxc6 11. Bf4 Nd7 12. Rc1 Ba6 13. Na4 Bb5 14. Nc3 Ba6 15.
Na4 Bb5 16. Nc3 Ba6 17. Na4 {"Before play started, W. Ritson Morry who, with R.
G. Wade, controlled, announced that the F.I.D.E. 30-move draw rule would be
strictly enforced. In little more than an hour this game had been officially
posted as drawn in 17 moves. Presumably the “spirit of conflict” had not
been offended, and neither player could depart from repetition." CHESS,
January 1964, p132} 1/2-1/2

